    "id": "70d41b6756f84554fb00a865",
    "path": "datafusion_spark::function::datetime::make_dt_interval::SparkMakeDtInterval::return_type",
    "name": "return_type",
    "owner": "datafusion_spark::function::datetime::make_dt_interval::SparkMakeDtInterval",
    "crate": "datafusion-spark",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn return_type(&self, _arg_types: &[DataType]) -> Result<DataType>",
    "docs": "Note the return type is `DataType::Duration(TimeUnit::Microsecond)` and not `DataType::Interval(DayTime)` as you might expect.\nThis is because `DataType::Interval(DayTime)` has precision only to the millisecond, whilst Spark's `DayTimeIntervalType` has\nprecision to the microsecond. We use `DataType::Duration(TimeUnit::Microsecond)` in order to not lose any precision. See the\n[Sail compatibility doc] for reference.\n\n[Sail compatibility doc]: https://github.com/lakehq/sail/blob/dc5368daa24d40a7758a299e1ba8fc985cb29108/docs/guide/dataframe/data-types/compatibility.md?plain=1#L260",
